    <metaInformation>
      <processInformation>
        <referenceFunction amount="1.0" category="metals" datasetRelatesToProduct="true" generalComment="The multi-output-process &quot;mining copper-ore&quot; delivers the co-products &quot;copper concentrate, at beneficiation&quot; and &quot;molybdenum, molybdenite concentrate, couple production Cu&quot;. The product &quot;copper concentrate&quot; is a intermediary process required in the following copper production (5.2.5 Winning of primary copper in ecoinvent). The module &quot;molybdenite concentrate&quot; is designed for the use in Ecoinvent as starting material for the manufacturing of molybdenum trioxide and ferromolybdenum, both materials which used in the manufacturing of high quality steels and alloys.;&#10;UUID: 75d60f1c-ae5b-3fc1-82d9-bf0b9bcc9824" includedProcesses="The module includes a mining and a beneficiation step with the mining infrastructure and disposal of overburden and tailings (see part II &quot;Auxiliary Processes&quot;)." infrastructureProcess="false" localCategory="metals" localName="Copper concentrate, at beneficiation" localSubCategory="non ferro" name="Copper concentrate, at beneficiation" subCategory="non ferro" unit="kg"/>
        <geography location="ID" text="This module is valid for the whole corresponding region. Some agents used like lime or sodium cyanide originate from data sets valid for Switzerland or Europe. Processes like blasting and transport originate from data sets valid for Switzerland or Europe."/>
        <technology text="Mining is done 70% open pit and 30% underground, followed by joint beneficiation of copper and molybdenite trough flotation, where considerable amounts of agents are added. Overburden and tailings are disposed near the mining site."/>
